{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And they placed him.</b> Alone — and they did not place the wood-gatherer with him, for both of them were in one chapter. They knew that the wood-gatherer was liable to death, but it had not been specified to them by what death; therefore it says (Numbers 15), ״כִּי לֹא פֹרַשׁ מַה יֵּעָשֶׂה לוֹ״. But concerning the blasphemer, He says to specify for them, for they did not know whether he was liable to death or not (Sifra; Sanhedrin 78)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:07.322853836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}